2026-10-18T18:38:55.9381302Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9389899Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9390328Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9390666Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9390853Z 
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9391002Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9391204Z 
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9391514Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9391997Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9392284Z 
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9392430Z If you would like to
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9392784Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9393024Z 
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9393273Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-18T18:38:55.9393745Z   $ sh ./install-nix
